Package: trialsurv
Title: Bayesian and Frequentist Time-to-Event Analysis of Clinical Trial Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("TrialSurv", "Authors", email = "maintainers@trialsurv.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A toolkit for the analysis of time-to-event endpoints in
    randomised clinical trials. It provides tidy loading of the colon cancer
    trial data, Kaplan-Meier estimation, Cox proportional hazards models with
    diagnostics and held-out concordance, a hierarchical Bayesian survival
    model that partially borrows information across treatment subgroups, a
    two-arm trial simulation engine for power and type I error, and an
    automated Quarto report that turns the results into a plain-language
    go/no-go recommendation.
